      "text": "```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport json\n\nresult = {}\n\nusecols = ['account_id', 'category', 'amount_cents']\ndtypes = {'account_id': 'int64', 'amount_cents': 'int64'}\n\nchunksize = 200_000\n\nfor chunk in pd.read_csv(\n    'transactions.csv',\n    usecols=usecols,\n    dtype=dtypes,\n    chunksize=chunksize\n):\n    mod = chunk['account_id'] % 11\n    mask = mod < 7\n    if not mask.any():\n        continue\n\n    sub_account = chunk.loc[mask, 'account_id']\n    sub_amount = chunk.loc[mask, 'amount_cents']\n    sub_category = chunk.loc[mask, 'category']\n\n    multiplier = (sub_account % 97) + 1\n\n    # Use Python's arbitrary precision integers to guarantee exact sums\n    # regardless of magnitude, avoiding any overflow issues with fixed-width ints.\n    amt_obj = sub_amount.astype(object)\n    mult_obj = multiplier.astype(object)\n\n    values = amt_obj * mult_obj\n\n    grouped = values.groupby(sub_category).sum()\n\n    for cat, val in grouped.items():\n        if cat in result:\n            result[cat] += int(val)\n        else:\n            result[cat] = int(val)\n\noutput = {k: result[k] for k in sorted(result.keys())}\nprint(\"TOTAL:\" + json.dumps(output))\n```",
